From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Date: Tue, 13 Jan 2026 11:52:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] CDX: Port to kernel 6.12 and suppress verbose boot messages

Kernel 6.12 compatibility:
- Update Makefile to use KERNEL_SRC for finding sdk_fman driver paths
- Fix include paths and kernel version detection
- Document ceetm_exit() cleanup requirements for module unload
- Fix various compiler warnings and unused variable warnings

Suppress verbose boot messages:
- Make DPAIPSEC_INFO and DPAWIFI_INFO macros conditional on CDX_DPA_DEBUG
- Change dpa_cfg.c printk() calls to use DPA_INFO under CDX_DPA_DEBUG
- Add misc.h include to dpa_wifi.c for CDX_DPA_DEBUG definition
- Wrap procfs.c, devman.c, vsp_cfg.c verbose prints in CDX_DPA_DEBUG

To re-enable verbose logging, uncomment CDX_DPA_DEBUG in misc.h or
add -DCDX_DPA_DEBUG to CFG_FLAGS in the recipe.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [kernel compatibility fix]
Signed-off-by: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>

